    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "HILLS ESTATE INCORPORATED,\nMills Building,\nSan Francisco.\nJanuary 28, 1927,\nJOSEPH J. PHILLIPS, ESQ.,\nRight of Way Agent, City and County of San Francisco,\nSan Franciseo, Callio mia.\nDear Sir:\n1111s Estate Incorporated is willing to lease to\nthe City and County of San Francisco, for use\nas a\ntemporazy almo lis property at san Bruno heretofore\none hundred and 112y 250) acres, oz\nthereabouts to you.\npointed out\nThe terms of the lease acceptable\nto us are as follows:\nThe lease 1s to run or a period of three (5)\nyears at a rental of Ten Dollars (910) an acre per year.\nThis Ten Dollars (910) per acre per year is arrived at as\nfollows:\nThe value of the loss of the pasturage each year\nis estimated at five Dollars (35),\nand the maintenance\ncharges amount to Five Dollars (5) a yeaz.\nIn addition to the foregoing payments, we aze to be\npaid the sum of Iwenty Five Dollars ($25) per acre at the\nend of the lease in order to recondition the land for the\npurposes for which it is now used.\nThis reconditioning\ninvolves the blowing, dising, harrowing and reseeding of\nthe property.\nme shal 1 maintain the levees during the term of the\nLease just as we have maintained them in the past, but any\ndamages that may result from any brealing of the levees, oz\nany other cause, must be borne by yourselves.\nwe understand that you desize to seed some parts\nif not all of the land in question, and it so such seeding\nas may be done must be with our consent in order that we may\nbe assured that no deleterious grasses will be grown on the\nproperty®\nAt the time being, we are maintaining and we shall\ncontinue the maintenance of a pumping plant for use in\nconnection with this land.\nAny addl tional expenses over and\nthose now borne by us for this punping that may be\noccasioned because of your requirements, will be borne by\nyou•\nYou will be adven permission to erect a water tank\non the adjacent property belonging to us, and to run a pipe",
      "line from that property to the land in question which Jou\nmay pipe as you see fit.\nUpon the termination of the lease, you are to\nremove any and all structures and improvements erected by you and\nforeign substances hauled to the property, such as cinders,\ngravel, etc., to make it available for our uses.\nIn making\nsuch removals you will be peritted to dump the\nwaste in the\nold borrow pit or sloughs on the property in question.\nTrusting that the foregoing will be of assistance to\nyou in establishing your temporary airport, we are,\nVery truly yours,\nMILIS ESTATE INCORPORATED\nBy Ogden Mi118•"
    ],
